IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`
IMPORT `mlr1-reg29-additional-cdd`

-- TESTS for regulation 29.  Expected values are written from the text (the line named in each heading).  Inputs are positional, in the order of the
-- function's GIVEN.  For the "must" functions each input is, in turn, a seam or paragraph answer ("gate"), a condition of the case ("where"), an "if" or
-- an "unless" exception; the helper generating these tests tries all true, then each input failing in turn.

§ `reg 29(1) and (2): where the regulation applies (src:878-879)`
#ASSERT `reg 29(1) this regulation applies` (LIST `credit institution`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 29(1) this regulation applies` (LIST `financial institution`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 29(1) this regulation applies` (LIST `estate agent`, `financial institution`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 29(1) this regulation applies` (LIST `estate agent`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 29(1) this regulation applies` (LIST `casino`, `auditor`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) arguments: the answer of regulation 3(1) for a contract of long-term insurance; the relevant person is providing a customer with that contract
#ASSERT `reg 29(2) paragraphs (3) to (5) apply` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 29(2) paragraphs (3) to (5) apply` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 29(2) paragraphs (3) to (5) apply` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 29(2) paragraphs (3) to (5) apply` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 29(2) paragraphs (3) to (5) apply` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `reg 29(3) to (5): beneficiaries of an insurance policy (src:880-884)`
